">Today you will research how zoos impact animals. You will read one article titled “The Stripes Will Survive.” Then you will read one passage titled “The Zoos Go Wild” and view one video <i>Behind the Scenes with the National Zoo’s Lion Cubs</i>. As you review these sources, you will gather information and answer questions about how zoos impact animals so you can write an essay.</p></div></div>\n    \t<div class=\"stimulus\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"passage-scrolling passage440\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"passageContent\" xml:base=\"VF557794.xml\"><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p id=\"psga_p001\">Watch this video titled “Behind the Scenes with the National Zoo’s Lion Cubs.” Then answer the questions.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-video\"><object data=\"assets/VF557794.v02.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"><param name=\"webmSource\" value=\"assets/VF557794.v02.webm\" valuetype=\"REF\"/></object></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"copyright-tm\" id=\"psga_p003\">Behind the Scenes with the National Zoo's Lion Cubs, copyright © 2013 by Smithsonian Institution. Used by permission.</p></div></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"span6\"><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><h4>Part A</h4></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"stem_paragraph\" id=\"p012\">Read the quotation from the video <em>Behind the Scenes with the National Zoo’s Lion Cubs.</em></p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"boxText\" id=\"p1111\">Caring for the cubs can be pretty challenging in that we have to stay away. (0:47) </p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"stem_paragraph\" id=\"p002\">How does the quotation contribute to the development of ideas in the video?</p></div><choiceInteraction class=\"choice_list\" maxChoices=\"1\" minChoices=\"1\" orientation=\"vertical\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE_A\" shuffle=\"false\"><simpleChoice identifier=\"rAi1\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p003\">It is used as an example of the challenges the curator faces at the zoo.</p></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier=\"rAi2\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p004\">It introduces how the lion cubs were cared for at the zoo.</p></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier=\"rAi3\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p005\">It is used to summarize the challenges the zoo faces. </p></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier=\"rAi4\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p006\">It explains why the zoo is unable to take care of the lion cubs.</p></simpleChoice></choiceInteraction><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><h4>Part B</h4></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"stem_paragraph\" id=\"p007\">Which detail from the video supports the answer to Part A?</p></div><choiceInteraction class=\"choice_list\" maxChoices=\"1\" minChoices=\"1\" orientation=\"vertical\" responseIdentifier=\"RESPONSE_B\" shuffle=\"false\"><simpleChoice identifier=\"rBi1\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p008\">“‘We’ve gone from having two females together and one male to having ten cats all together in one big pride.’” (0:39)</p></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier=\"rBi2\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p009\">“‘The initial desire of everybody is to run and put your hands on them to see how they feel, to see what their health is like, when in reality the best thing for the cubs, especially just after they’re born, is to leave them with mom . . . .’” (0:54)</p></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier=\"rBi3\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p010\">“‘One of my jobs as the curator is to work very closely with veterinarians.’” (1:21)</p></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier=\"rBi4\"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"p011\">“‘We’ve had not only one litter of lions born, but we’ve had two litters of lions born—you just feel like, “Wow!”’” (2:56)</p></simpleChoice></choiceInteraction></div>\n</div></itemBody><responseProcessing template=\"1A1+E\"><responseCondition><responseIf><equal><mapResponse identifier=\"RESPONSE_B\"/><default identifier=\"allCorrect_B\"/></equal><setOutcomeValue identifier=\"SCORE_B\"><baseValue baseType=\"float\">1</baseValue></setOutcomeValue></responseIf><responseElse><setOutcomeValue identifier=\"SCORE_B\"><baseValue baseType=\"float\">0</baseValue></setOutcomeValue></responseElse></responseCondition><responseCondition><responseIf><equal><mapResponse identifier=\"RESPONSE_A\"/><default identifier=\"allCorrect_A\"/></equal><setOutcomeValue identifier=\"SCORE_A\"><baseValue baseType=\"float\">1</baseValue></setOutcomeValue><setOutcomeValue identifier=\"SCORE\"><baseValue baseType=\"float\">1</baseValue></setOutcomeValue><responseCondition><responseIf><equal><variable identifier=\"SCORE_B\"/><baseValue baseType=\"float\">1</baseValue></equal><setOutcomeValue identifier=\"SCORE\"><baseValue baseType=\"float\">2</baseValue></setOutcomeValue></responseIf></responseCondition></responseIf><responseElse><setOutcomeValue identifier=\"SCORE\"><baseValue baseType=\"float\">0</baseValue></setOutcomeValue></responseElse></responseCondition></responseProcessing></assessmentItem>"
